Groton Massachusetts Middlesex Co - Oct 8 th 1838 -
Dear Sir;
I have received the Pension Certificate of Eunice Thorning widow of William Thorning granting her Thirty Dollars per annum. - - $ 1 / 2 William Thorning, who was a Pensioner under Act 10 th March 1818, proved only nine months service, which was necessary for him to have obtained a pension, I supposed, that his widow would have rec d  1 / 2 of the sum he rec d under that Act, which would be equivalent to what he would have rec d had he have drawn under Act 7 June 1832 - - which would have given her $36 - instead of $30, how will it oblige me, by informing me why it was not thus determined - -
Will you also inform me if the names Solomon Spaulding & Thomas Wheeler are found enrolled in the company of Capt Joshua Parker & Colo. Reads Regiment during the year 1777 - Capt Parker belonged to Guilford in this County - I would also enquire, if more service than that proved by William Thorning, can now be proved, will the pension of his widow be proportionately increased -
Respectfully Yours Geo. F. Bruntwell
J. S. Edwards Esq. - Washington D. C. - }

