Sir;
In the case of Lydia, widow of Paul Landerskiu, dec'd., to whom was issued certificate No. 4881, Augusta, Maine, roll, I respectfully submit that the widow is entitled to a pension of $96 00 per Annum, from February 3 rd 1853, instead of $22 66 .
Daniel Landerskiu received $96 00 per Annum under the Acts of 1818 and subsequent Acts for service as a mariner &c. in 1775-6, covering a period of fifteen months' service in the Revolutionary War, and said Pension was paid him up to the date of his death. His widow is entitled under the Acts of 1848 and 1853 to receive a pension equal in amount to that received by her husband, and a grievous error was committed in not allowing her $96 00 .

