On this 16 th day of March 1850 before me William P. Minor a justice of the peace in and for said County personally appeared Abigail Mead a resident of the Town of Greenwich in said County. Aged eighty two Years who being first duly sworn according to law doth on her oath make the following Declaration in order to obtain an increase of pension which she is informed and believes was due her husband Levi Mead under the Act of Congress passed June 7 th 1832 That she is the widow of Levi Mead deceased who was a private soldier in the War of the Revolution and a pensioner of the United States at the rate of twenty four Dollars and Twenty two cents per Annum and died on the twenty sixth day of May one thousand eight hundred and forty nine That she has been informed by her Husband and others that her Husband aforesaid served in the State of Connecticut and also under officers in the State of New York during the Revolutionary War. That she has reason to believe the last named service was not computed in the adjustment of her Husband's pension and for which she now claims an increase of his pension. In support of which she refers the pension Department to the evidence on file as well as to such as may be furnished by her Agent William Valentine of Albany. She further declares that she is still a widow. Subscribed & sworn to before me } this 16 th day of March 1850 }
before me William P. Minor Justice of the Peace
