I, Orson Benjamin, surrogate of said County do hereby certify that Silas Phelps late of the town of Manchester said County deceased was a United States Pensioner inscribed on the Pension Roll of the New York Albany Agency at the rate of One hundred and twenty dollars per annum, and that he died at Manchester aforesaid on the twenty third day of February last (1833) leaving a widow still surviving whose name is Mary Phelps, and who has made application for a pension hereto attached. All which appears satisfactory to this Court on the oaths of John Thompson and Margaret Moores & Lyman Clark.
In testimony whereof I have hereto set my hand and affixed the seal of said Court at Canandaigua this second day of June A.D. 1855. Orson Benjamin Surrogate
