On this 12th day of April A.D. 1874 before me, xxx  Amos D. Larned  xxx a Justice of the Peace  xxx in and for said county, duly authorized by law to administer oaths, personally appeared Frances Barnes wife of William P. Barnes a resident of Fowler in the county of Trumbull and state of Ohio, aged 68, who being duly sworn according to law, declares on her said oath, that she is a daughter and heir at law of the identical Anthony Remington who was pensioned at the rate of $60 per annum under the act of Congress of March 18, 1818 for services in the Revolutionary War as a Marine from the State of Rhode Island, and whose name was inscribed on the Pension Roll of the State of Massachusetts and paid at the Agency of Hartford in the state of Connecticut; and, also, that she is daughter and heir at law of the identical Hannah Remington whose name was inscribed on the Pension Roll of the State of Ohio, under the act of Congress of July, 7, 1838, as the widow of the above named Anthony Remington, and on account of his services, at the rate of $40.00 per annum, payable at the Pittsburgh Agency in the State of Pennsylvania.
