On this 21 st day of March A.D. 1858, before the subscriber, a Justice of the Peace in and for the County aforesaid, duly authorized by law to administer oaths, personally appeared Lucy Shurtliff, aged seventy nine years, a resident of Middlebury in said County and State, and made oath in due form of law that she is the widow of Benoni Shurtliff, late of said Middlebury, deceased, who was a Private and Marine in the Revolutionary war, and subsequently a Pensioner of the United States, under the Act of June 7 th 1832, at the rate of Eighty Dollars per annum, inscribed on the Vermont Roll; that the said Benoni died in said Middlebury on the 6 th day of February 1841; that she has not intermarried since the death of said Benoni, but continues his widow; that she is a Pensioner of the United States, under the 2 nd Section of the Act of February 3 rd 1859, at the rate of Sixty Six Dollars and Sixty six cents per annum, inscribed on the Vermont Roll, Burlington Agency; that she is informed and believes that she is entitled, by virtue of the 3 rd Section of the Act of February 28 th 1855, to receive a higher rate of Pension than that which she now receives: to obtain which higher rate she makes this declaration.
And the said declarant hereby constitutes Messrs Weston & Shaw, of Burlington Vermont, her Attorneys with power of substitution, to investigate and substantiate her said claim for an increase of Pension, and to do any act or thing necessary to be done to obtain the allowance thereof, hereby ratifying and confirming whatever her said Attorneys may lawfully do in the premises.
In witness whereof, she does hereunto set her hand and seal at Middlebury aforesaid, on the day and year first above mentioned - The words "higher rate, she makes this declaration", interlined. Signed sealed & delivered above before signing -
In presence of W. H. Parker } J. K. L. Smith }
