In order to obtain the benefits of the resolution of Congress of the 23 rd January, 1845. Whereas the act of the 30 th of April, 1844 prohibited me from drawing a pension for the same period during which my husband was a pensioner. I now make the following statement under oath, to obtain the benefits of the resolution above mentioned. I am the widow of Hosea Sprague who was a private in the war of the Revolution. I have drawn a pension at the rate of fifty dollars per annum from the 20 th day of November 1843 and now ask for the amount due me from the 1 st day of March 1836 to the 20 th day of November 1843 when my former pension commenced.
Elizabeth Sprague
