In this sixteenth day of September in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and forty three personally appeared in open Court of Common Pleas in and for said County Mrs Eliza Alden now a resident of Mudville in said State formerly a resident of West Point State of New York, aged forty six years who being first duly sworn ac- cording to law, doth on her oath state that she is the widow of the late Roger Alden who was a pensioner of the United States up to the day of his death, on the New York agency, at the rate of $480 per annum as Captain and aid, and after the death of said Roger the balance of pension due to him was paid to me, as his widow, as will be shown by evidence deposited at the time payment was made. Now the object of this declaration being made is in order to assert a claim as widow under act of June 1832 in right of said Roger Alden to an increased pension as aid-de-camp at the rate of $50 per month, from the 4 th March 1831 up to the time of his death which took place on the 10 th October 1836 The said Roger having served it is believed for upward of two years as Capt and aid, as will more particularly be shown by his own statement of service now on file under act of 1832. To those papers respectful reference is made.
