She further declares that she was married to the said Joseph Brown 2 d in the month of February one thousand seven hundred and eighty-eight, in the town of Cambridge, County of Washington, and State of New York, by a preacher of the Baptist order, whose name was William Wait: That her husband the aforesaid Joseph Brown 2 d died in the town of Northampton, State and County aforesaid on the twenty-ninth day of June, one thou- sand eight hundred and forty six, and that the arrears of Pension due at the time of his death, have been paid from the 4 th of March 1846, to the 29 th day of June 1846, in consequence of which the original certificate of Pension of the said Joseph Brown 2 d has been surrendered up. That she was not married to him prior to his leaving the service, but the marriage took place previous to the first of January seventeen hundred and ninety-four, viz: at the time above stated; therefore she hereby claims a Pension, (by virtue of the above recited Acts of Congress,) from the twenty ninth day of June one thousand eight hundred and forty six, until the day of her death;

