State of Pennsylvania } County of Crawford }
On this 23 d day of August, 1851 in Open Court of Common Pleas held in and for said county personally appeared George Camp aged 53 years resident in Cuscarawgo Township in said County of Crawford, who being first duly sworn according to law doth on his oath make the following declaration under the act of Congress passed on the 7 July 1838 & subsequent acts.
This declarant states that he is the lawful child of Casper Camp late of said county who was a revolutionary pensioner of the United States under the act of 18 March 1818 at the rate of $96 per annum, and who died on the third (3 d ) day of October in the year eighteen hundred and thirty six (1836). This declarant states that he is the lawful child of Christiana Camp who was the lawful wife & widow of the aforesaid Casper; that the maiden name of the declarant's mother was Christiana Schwartz; that the said Christiana & Casper Camp were lawfully married in the county of Berks in the State of Pennsylvania in the year seventeen hundred and eighty three (1783), that the said Casper & Christiana had five children born as the fruits of their said marriage who were born prior to the year seventeen hundred & ninety four (1794) and whose names are John, Jacob, Christiana, Mary Ann, & Elizabeth Camp. This declarant states that the records hereto annexed are the original records of the ages of the children of the said Casper & Christiana Camp; the ages of two of said children being thereon written. That said records have been held in the possession of the family of the said Casper & Christiana Camp ever since the time they were made, and are believed to be correct. This declarant further states that the said Casper & Christiana Camp lived in lawful wedlock as man & wife from the time of their aforesaid marriage up to the period when she died, and that after the death of the said Casper his said widow did not again marry.

