years, and no part of said sum has ever been rec d by the Widow of said Ezra or any of his heirs, and that the same has been withheld unjustly thro' false & wicked reports. The Pension then was $96 per Annum. He the said Ezra being an artificer, it was ascertained, that he was entitled to $144 per year instead of $96. The extra $48 per year, was granted to his Widow Eunice Clark from the time he commenced drawing, viz from March 31 st 1818 to the time that the application was made for said extra Pension, (except the three years, as above stated,) and she, the said Eunice Clark continued to receive the above sum of $144 per year until her death.
