On this fifth day of September A.D. 1864, personally appeared before the undersigned, one of the Judges of the Court of Common Pleas, in and for the County and State aforesaid, Esther or Kitty Davis, a resident of the Township of North Amboy, in the County of Middlesex, and State of New Jersey, aged Sixty one years, who first being duly sworn according to law, doth on her oath make the following declaration, in order to obtain the benefits of the provisions made by the act of Congress, passed on the 3 rd day of February, 1853, granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the Revolutionary war; That she is the widow of Edward Davis, who was a Revolutionary pensioner of the United States, at Ninety Six dollars per annum, first of the New Jersey Agency, and afterwards of the City of New York under the act, (as she believes) of the 18 th of March 1818; - that she does not know, but believes his service was as a marine on board the Frigate Boston.
She further declares, that she was married to the said Edward Davis, or Edward E. Davis, as he sometimes called himself, at Gambery, in the County of Middlesex, and State of New Jersey, by one James J. Woodhull, a Minister of the gospel, on the 22 nd day of October, A.D. One thousand eight hundred and fourteen; of which there is public record, in the office of the County Clerk, of Middlesex County, New Jersey; She further declares, that her maiden name, was Esther, or Kitty Gorton;

