STATE OF Virginia COUNTY OF Buckingham } ss.
On this 9 th day of July , 185 5 , personally appeared before me a Justice of the peace, Alexander Hammond and Alex. Pendleton , who, being first duly sworn according to law, declare that Elizabeth Hallwell is the widow of James Hallwell decd. who was a Revolutionary Soldier and Pensioner of the United States, and received some twenty dollars per annum during his life time - that they were personally acquainted with said Hallwell for many years before his death - and that they are also well acquainted with his widow Elizabeth Hallwell who is now applying for pension;
That said Revolutionary soldier died in the County of Buckingham and State of Virginia on the 15 th day of August in the year 1799, and that the said Elizabeth Hallwell was married to him, the said James Hallwell in the County of Buckingham State of Virginia on the 15 th day of August in the year 1799, and that previous thereto her name was Elizabeth Morgan and they declare that they have derived the above information in regard to said service, marriage and death of said Revolutionary soldier, in the following manner, viz: In regard to service, from having known him as a Pensioner; - Marriage from common report - & from all the time since, and date of his death from a newspaper in his immediate neighborhood ; and that they were present and saw Mrs. Elizabeth Hallwell sign her name to the foregoing declaration for pension, &c;
They further declare that the applicant is still a widow, and that they are disinterested in making these affidavits.
Alexander Hammond Alex. Pendleton
Sworn and subscribed the day and year above written; and it is hereby certified that the affiants are credible persons and are aged the former 70 years, and the latter 70 years; that they are known to me as residents of said County and State and that I am disinterested in this claim. Richd B. Pennington J.P.

