On this Fourth day of October 1848 personally appeared before me Nathaniel Hyatt a Justice of the Peace in and for said County Susan Ferris a resident of Bedford in said County who being first duly sworn according to law, doth on her oath make the following Declaration in order to obtain the benefits of the provision made by the Resolution of Congress of July 1 st 1848 — That she is the widow of John Ferris who in his lifetime was a pensioner of the United States at the rate of Eighty Dollars per Annum under the Act of June 7 th 1832 That she has heretofore made application for a pension & has been informed & believes that her claim has not been granted for want of record evidence of her said husband's military service and having been informed that the objection to the admission of her claim is now removed by said Resolution of Congress of July 1 st 1848 she now renews her application and claims the same amount per Annum as received by her husband upon the proof on file in the Pension Office and under said Resolution, as also under the various laws under which she has heretofore applied or may be entitled. In support of which claim she refers the pension Department to the proof on file & to said Resolution of Congress. She further declares that she is now a widow — Subscribed & Sworn to before } on this Fourth day of October 1848 } Susan the Ferris Nathaniel Hyatt Justice of the Peace } mark
