On this Twelfth day of April 1833 before me a Magistrate in and for said District personally appeared Sally Finley who being duly sworn declares, that she is the widow of John Finley deceased, who was at resident of the said State and District and was a Revolutionary Pensioner of the United States at the rate of Sixty Dollars per annum for the term of his natural life; That the said John Finley died at Abbeville Court House on the nineteenth day of December one thousand eight hundred and thirty six; That her maiden name was Callie Posey and that she was married to the said John Finley on the twenty fifth day of December anno Domini one thousand eight hundred and eight in Abbeville District by the Revd Arthur Williams a Baptist minister; That the said John Finley was pensioned under the act of Congress passed on the seventh day of June one thousand eight hundred and thirty two; That she has remained a widow since the death of her said husband; That she is a resident of the said State & District, and makes this declaration for the benefit of the act of Congress passed February the third one thousand eight hundred and fifty three; That she appoints B. L. Posey her true and lawful Attorney to demand and receive the Pension certificate to which she may be entitled; For proof of her marriage see copy of Private Record in her possession herewith exhibited.
Signed in presence of Samrod Richey B. V. Rose Sally Finley mark

State of Illinois } Clark county. }
I Stephen Archer, Judge, of the Probate court in and for the county of Clark and state of Illinois holden at Marshall, do hereby certify, that Satisfactory evidence has been exhibited and given to said court, that Sarah Finney, was an applicant for a pension, as the widow of John Finney, who was a pensioner of the United States, at the rate of forty dollars per annum, — and died in the county of Rush and state of Indiana, where he resided, on the 11 th day of July 1836. That the said Sarah Finney, his widow resided in the county of Rush and state of Indiana, and died in the county of Rush and state of Indiana on the 4 th day of October 1848. That she left an only child who is now living, whose name is Amos Finney:
In testimony whereof, I have hereunto set my hand and affixed my seal of office at Marshall this 9 th day of April in the year of our Lord 1849. Stephen Archer Judge Justice of the Peace

