On this 1 st day of March 1849 before David C Churchill an associate Justice of the Court of Common Pleas within and for the County of Grafton and State of New Hampshire, personally appeared Annollansbee a resident of Enfield in said County aged upwards of 87 years, who being first duly sworn according to Law doth on her oath make the following declaration in order to obtain the benefit of the act of Congress of the 17 th of June 1844 and of the Joint Resolution of July 1. 1848 entitled, "A Joint Resolution relative to evidence in applications for Pensions."
That she is the widow of Nathanollansbee who was a New Hampshire Pensioner of the United States under the Act of the 7 th June 1832 at the rate of Twenty Seven Dollars and ninety eight Cents per annum. That she was married to the said Nathanollansbee at Plaistow in the County of Rockingham and State of New Hampshire a town adjoining Haverhill Massachusetts by the Rev. Giles Merrill who she believes was pastor of Churches in each of said towns on the eleventh day of December seventeen hundred and eighty three, her family name being Ann Sawyer. That her husband the said Nathanollansbee died at said Enfield on the twenty sixth day of December eighteen hundred forty seven; and that he was at the time of his death a New Hampshire Pensioner of the United States under the Act of the 7 th June 1832, at the rate of $27.98 per annum. See the accompanying Certificate of the Clerk of the North Church in North Haverhill Massachusetts

