On this third day of June July A.D. 1834 personally appeared before me the subscribing authority Martha Forbes a resident of Stockholm in the County and State aforesaid, aged seventy one years, who first being duly sworn according to Law doth on her oath make the following declaration in order to obtain the benefits of the provision made by the act of Congress passed on the 3 d of February A.D. 1833 granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the Revolutionary War; that she is the widow of Samuel Forbes who was a private in the Massachusetts Continental Line and was placed on the New York Pensions Roll March 8 th A.D. 1833 at the rate of Forty-three Dollars and thirty-three cents per annum.
