On this 6 th day of September , 185 5 , personally appeared before * me a Justice of the Peace for said County , Mrs Sarah Frazier , a resident of said County and State, aged 64 years, who, being first duly sworn according to law, doth, on her oath make the following declaration, in order to obtain the benefits of the provision made by the Act of Congress, passed on the 3 o day of † February , 18 53 , granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the Revolutionary war: That she is the widow of Lowell Frazier who was a † Private Soldier in the North Carolina Militia in the Revolutionary War, and who for his services was pensioned by the United States at $20. per annum for some years before his death; and for proof of his service she now refers to his old pension papers now on file at Washington &c;
she further declares that she was married to the said Lowell Frazier on the 29 th day of April , in the year (1833) Eighteen hundred and Thirty Three in the County of Stokes and State of North Carolina by one Jubal Alda a Justice of the Peace duly authorized by law to administer the rites of matrimony, and that her name previous to marriage was Sarah Davis ; and that she has no other proof of said marriage than that herewith presented: that her said husband died in the County of Forsyth State of North Carolina on the 18 th day of March , 18 51 ; that she was not married to him prior to the year hundred and Thirty Three but at the time above stated. She further declares that
she is still a widow, and that she has never before made application for pension under this or any other act of Congress, and has no record of marriage to attest: Inv. H. H. H. H.  Sarah Frazier attest: Cyrus H. Whicko
