On this eighth day of August AD 1844 personally appeared before John W. Smith a justice of the Peace in and for said Orange County Betsey Frink a resident of the Town of Royalton in the County of Windsor & State aforesaid. Aged 76 years who being first duly sworn according to Law doth on her oath make the following de- claration in order to obtain the benefits of the Act of June 17. 1844. Entitled an act to Continue the Pensions of Certain widows That she is the widow of Willard Frink deceased who was a private in the war of the Revolution, and drew as set forth in his declaration under the Act of 1818. and her declaration under the five years act & one years act - that her husband's pension was 96 dollars per annum and that her pension was $56.61 - that in consequence of his said death she this declarant has already applied for & received a pension at the rate of $56.61 per annum under the Acts of July 7. 1838 and March 3. 1843. - She further declares that she is still a Widow Witness her hand Betsey Frink John W. Smith
