On this eighth day of December 1848 personally appeared before the subscriber, a Justice of the Peace in and for said County, Eliza B. Woodbury, a child and daughter of Jane Gordon, lately a resident of Bedford in said County of Hillsborough deceased, who being first, duly sworn according to Law, doth on her oath make the following declaration, in order to obtain the benefits of the provision made by the Act of Congress, passed on the 2 nd February, 1848 granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the Revolutionary War; That the said Jane Gordon was the Widow of Josiah Gordon who was a private in the Revolution, That the said Jane Gordon was a pensioner and received a pension under the Act of 17 th June 1844, at the rate of twenty nine Dollars and eighty nine cents per annum - That she died at said Bedford on the 29 th day of May Anno Domini 1848 That she left three children living viz. Adam Gordon Eliza B. Woodbury wife of Peter K. Woodbury and Jane Gordon they being all and the only surviving children. She further declares that the said Jane Gordon was a Widow at the time of her death. Eliza B. Woodbury sworn and subscribed on the day and year above written
