On the fifth day of May A.D. One thousand eight hundred and fifty four personally appeared before the Subscribers one of the Judges of the Court of Common Pleas (a Court of Record) for the County of Dauphin Mary Gray, a resident of Swatara Township in the County of Dauphin and State of Pennsylvania, aged Eighty three years, who being duly sworn according to Law, doth on her oath make the following declaration in order to obtain the benefit of the provisions made by the Act of Congress passed July 29. 1848 & its supplements viz - That she is the Widow of Robert Gray, late of the County and State aforesaid, who was a private and Ensign in the Army of the Revolution, and as such received in his lifetime a certificate of pension from the United States, bearing date the 25 th of February A.D. 1833 in the sum of Forty four \frac{8}{100} Dollars per annum, as by the said original certificate in her possession, and purporting to be recorded at the proper office in Washington City in "Book D. Vol. 6 page 59" well more fully appear. She further declares that she was married to the said Robert Gray on the day of June - in the year of our Lord Seventeen hundred and ninety, but that she has no record proof of her said marriage, nor does she know of any person now living who was present at, and can testify to the fact of the said marriage, and she is therefore obliged to transmit to the Department, as the best evidence in her power, the depositions of some of the oldest inhabitants of the neighbourhood who testify their knowledge in regard to the matter; that her Husband the aforesaid Robert Gray, died on the twenty seventh day of April A.D. Eighteen hundred and forty eight; that she was not married to him prior to his leaving the service but the marriage took place previous to the Second of January A.D. Eighteen hundred viz. at or about the time above stated. She further states that she is now a widow, and has been such ever since the death of her said Husband; and that she has never before made any application for a pension.
Sworn & subscribed the day & year above written, before me } Mary I do hereby certify that the said Mary Gray cannot } by reason of bodily infirmity attend the Court. }
J. A. Heister Judge
Mary Gray

