State of New York } County of Delaware }
On this 21 st day of June personally appeared before the Delaware County Court of the state of New York Esther Grant a resident of Haverhill in the County of Delaware and State aforesaid, being first duly sworn, to wit: That she is the widow of the late Nicholas Grant, who at the time of his death was entitled to certain benefits of the Pension made by the act of Congress passed on the 3 rd March 1818 granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the Revolutionary War; that she is the widow of Nicholas Grant who was a soldier in the War of the Revolution and a pensioner of the United States at the time of his death at the rate of Twenty Dollars per annum. She further states and declares that she was married to the said Nicholas Grant on the 11 th day of February Eighteen hundred and one, that her said husband died on the 6 th day of May Eighteen hundred and five, that she was not married to him prior to the second of January Eighteen hundred, but at the time when she married him she was a widow.
Witness my hand Wm Cason Jr. County Judge of Delaware County New York.

