On this 29 th day of June, 1853, personally appeared before the undersigned a Justice of the peace of the County and State of Kentucky, Margart Ann Grove a resident of Jefferson County, Kentucky aged about eighty eight years who first being duly sworn according to law, doth, on her oath make the following declaration in order to obtain the benefits of the provisions made by the act of Congress passed on the 3 rd February, 1853, granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the Revolutionary War; That she is the widow of John Grove dec d . who was a wagon conductor in the Revolutionary War, and who was entitled to four hundred and eighty dollars per annum, as will appear by reference, which is herewith made to the papers on file in the Pension Department at Washington City and upon which a certificate issued on the 24 th day of May, 1853, made payable to this declarant, for the said sum of $480- per annum.
She further declares that she is blind, and very infirm in other respects, and physically unable to go to the County Seat which is eighteen miles distant and make this declaration in open court. She also declares that she still remains a widow - that her husband said Grove died 11 th Dec r 1848. and that she was married to said Grove on the

