On This 23 rd day of March, One Thousand Eight hundred and fifty Three, personally appeared before The Inferior Court of the County and State aforesaid, Elendor Guest, a resident of said County, aged fifty four years, who being duly sworn according to law, doth, on her oath, make the following declaration in order to obtain the benefit of the provisions made by the Act of Congress, passed 3 rd February 1853;
That she is the widow of Moses Guest, who was a pensioner of the United States at the rate of Two hundred and Eighty dollars per annum; That her said husband Moses Guest resided in Franklin County, State of Georgia at the time he received said pension, and that his said pension was paid at the Georgia Agency at Savannah.
She further declares that she was married to the said Moses Guest on the Eighth day of May Eighteen hundred and twenty nine; That her husband the aforesaid Moses Guest died on the first day of October in the year Eighteen hundred and thirty Eight; That she was married to him at the time above stated. She further swears that she was a widow at the passage of the act, and is still a widow, and that she has never before made application for a pension.
Sworn to and subscribed the day and year } above written before }
