On this fifteenth 15 th day of August Eighteen hundred and forty five 1845. before me the Subscriber a Justice of the Inferior Court in and for Said County and State aforesaid the same being a Court of Record, Personally appeared Elizabeth Guice a resident of Said County and State aforesaid aged Seventy seven 77 years past who being duly sworn according to law doth on her oath make the following declaration In order to obtain the benefit of the several acts of Congress applicable to her case. That she is the Widow of John Guice who died on the Twenty sixth day of September Eighteen hundred and forty one 1841, in Meriwether County State of Georgia and That she is still his widow and That the said John Guice was a pensioner of the United States at the time of his death and for several years before does not know what act he drew a pension under on the Roll of the Georgia agency and deponent refers to the Declarations and Certificates all ready filed in pension office of the certainty of his service as a Revolutionary soldier length of time he served Rank and grade he held in the army and the amount he received yearly or per annum And deponent further declares That she was Legally married to the said John Guice on the last day of January Seventeen hundred and eighty six 1786. Ceremony Solomnized by Dr. Smith a Baptist preacher in Wilkes County afterwards cut off in Lincoln County State of Georgia

