On this 26 th day of Sept 1851 before me Spring Fowler a Justice of the Peace in and for said County personally appeared Sally P Holliday of Senex Madison County & State of New York who being duly sworn according to law deposes & says that she is the daughter of Martha Handy, Widow of William Handy, who was a Revolutionary pensioner of the United States. That at the time of her death she was on the roll of the Albany Agency at the rate of $144 per Annum. That she died on the 12 th day of August 1843, and left the following surviving Child viz - Sally P Holliday to wit this deponent and that no administrator was ever appointed — Now the object of this declaration is to assert a claim to an increase of pension to which it is believed that the said Martha Handy was entitled at the time of her death —
Sworn & Subscribed before me } this 26 th day of Sept 1851 }
Sally P Holliday
Spring Fowler } Just of the Peace }

