On this Twentieth day of August in the Year of our Lord One thousand eight hundred and forty-four, personally appeared before me Emanuel Reigart Esquire, an Alderman in and for said City of Lancaster in the State aforesaid Margaret Hartman, a resident of the City of Lancaster in the County & State aforesaid, aged Seventy-nine Years, who being first duly sworn according to law doth on her oath, make the following Declaration, in order to obtain the benefits of the provision made by the act of Congress, passed the 3 rd day of March, 1843, granting pensions to widows of persons, who served during the Revolutionary war. That she is the widow of Jacob Hartman who was a private soldier in the army of the revolution, agreeably to the facts in her original statement & Declaration, and that as such widow, she received and drew a pension from the United States Government at the rate of Eighty Dollars per annum, under the provisions of the Act of Congress of July 7, 1838.
