On this 8th day of June 1852 before the subscriber a Justice of the Peace within and for said County personally appeared Jerusha Hartshorn, widow of Aaron Hartshorn a resident of Cambridge in said County who being first duly sworn according to law doth on her oath make the following renewed declaration in order to an increase of the Pension that was granted her on the 20th day of December 1851 under the act of July 7. 1838 and the subsequent acts at the rate of Twenty Six Dollars and Sixty Six cents per annum. That at the time of the settlement of her claim as above stated she was allowed for but a part of the service rendered by her late husband Aaron Hartshorn as she understands and believes, to wit, for eight months as a Massachusetts Private in 1775 when he was a resident of Andover Massachusetts.
That at the time of making her original declaration she was unable to describe definitely the several tours of service that her husband rendered, nor can she now do it, and at this time furnish evidence thereof but is confident from what she has heard her husband and others say that he actually did perform a tour of three months or more at New York in 1776 but whether under Massachusetts or New Hampshire officers she is unable to state but is of the belief that he went as a New Hampshire man, for after the expiration of his eight months service in 1775 he removed from Andover Massachusetts and took up his abode in Goudon near Concord in the State of New Hampshire where she first became acquainted with him in 1776 he being then a

