District of Canterbury } p. Probate Office County of Windham }
On this 30 th day of May 1843, personally appeared before the Court of Probate within and for the district of Canterbury, Olive Henrik, a resident of said town of Canterbury, aged 80 years who being first duly sworn according to Law, doth on her oath, make the following declarations, in order to obtain the benefits of the provisions made by the act of Congress passed on the 3 rd day of March 1843 granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the revolutionary war.
That she is the widow of Daniel Henrik formerly of said Canterbury, now deceased, who was a private in the army of the revolution and served as stated in my former declaration for a pension, under the law of Congress of the 7 th of July 1838, on file in the office of the Commissioner of pensions reference being had thereto, as well as to the proof accompanying the same. This Applicant having received a pension for five years under said last mentioned law of the sum of $40.00 per annum she doth now further declare that she is still a widow. Olive Henrik

