State of North Carolina } Wilkes County }
Be it Known that on the 1 st day of November AD 1854 in Open Court, it being a Court of Record there in Session, personally appeared Alfred Six of said County and, state aforesaid who after being duly sworn states that he is the administrator upon the estate of Mary Six deceased late of said County and state who was a pensioner of the United States at the rate of forty Dollars per annum that the said Mary Six died on the 12 th day of June 1853. The said Mary Six was the widow of Mercajak Six deceased late of said County, who was a pensioner of the United States at the rate of ninety six Dollars per annum, and he is advised and believes that the said Mary Six was entitled to full pay or pension under the several acts and Resolutions of Congress granting pensions to the widows of Revolutionary soldiers he makes this statement to recover the balance of her pension due up to the time of her death.
Sworn to in open Court the 1 st day of November 1854 W. Mastin Clk Alfred + Six mothers
