State of New York }
Livingston County } ss.
On this sixth day of March one thousand eight hundred and forty four personally appeared before me Lewis W. Beecher a Justice of the peace in and for the County of Livingston residing in the town of Row in said County, Elizabeth Howe a resident of the town of Row in the County of Livingston aged Seventy, 84 years on the tenth day of December last past who being first duly sworn acc to law doth on her oath make the following declarations, in order to obtain the benefit of the provision made by the Act of Congress passed on the 3 March 1843. granting pensions to widows of persons who served during the Revolutionary War - That she is the widow of Selah Howe who was private in the army of the Revolution, as appears by his certificates of pension bearing date the tenth day of April one thousand eight hundred and twenty three now in the possession of this deponent - And this deponent further saith that the annual amount of the pension which she received under the act of July 7. 1838. was eighty dollars per annum - And she further declares that she is still a widow.
Sworn to and subscribed in the day and year above written before Elizabeth J. Howe
Lewis W. Beecher Justice of the peace
